The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    protected function session()
    {
        return app('session.store');
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Illuminate\Tests\Testing\TestResponseTest::testAssertJsonSerializedSessionHasErrors`:
            
```php
    public function testAssertJsonSerializedSessionHasErrors()
    {
        app()->instance('session.store', $store = new Store('test-session', new ArraySessionHandler(1), null, 'json'));

        $store->put('errors', $errorBag = new ViewErrorBag);

        $errorBag->put('default', new MessageBag([
            'foo' => [
                'foo is required',
            ],
        ]));

        $store->save(); // Required to serialize error bag to JSON

        $response = TestResponse::fromBaseResponse(new Response());

        $response->assertSessionHasErrors(['foo']);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Call to a member function getBag() on array
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
